uca sexta </italic>with non-pathogenic <italic>Escherichia coli </italic>elicits immunity to pathogenic <italic>Photorhabdus luminescens</italic>: roles of immune-related proteins shown by RNA interference</article-title><source>Insect Biochem Mol Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>517</fpage><lpage>525</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16731347</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ibmb.2006.04.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eleftherianos</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Millichap</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>ffrench-Constant</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynolds</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RNAi suppression of recognition protein mediated immune responses in the tobacco hornworm <italic>Manduca sexta </italic>causes increased susceptibility to the insect pathogen <italic>Photorhabdus</italic></article-title><source>Dev Comp Immunol</source><year>2006</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1099</fpage><lpage>1107</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16620974</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.dci.2006.02.008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Held</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Larock</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Argenio</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A metalloprotease secreted by the insect pathogen <italic>Photorhabdus luminescens </italic>induces melanization</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>7622</fpage><lpage>7628<